{
    "title": "Train your Brain - Attention",
    "description": "We present this game collection to stimulate attention and to train concentration. Fun games to stimulate your brain in a playful way. This focus game is suitable for the whole family, from the youngest to the elderly and senior players.\r\n\r\nTYPES OF GAMES\r\n\r\n- Puzzles \r\n- Labyrinths\r\n- Word Search\r\n- Association of colors and words\r\n- Find the differences\r\n- Find objects\r\n- Find the intruder\r\n\r\nIn addition to attention, these games help to stimulate other areas such as visual association, fine motor skills, visual memory or orientation.\r\n\r\nAPP FEATURES\r\n\r\nDaily attention training\r\nAvailable in 5 languages\r\nSimple and intuitive interface\r\nDifferent levels for all ages\r\nConstant updates with new games\r\n\r\nGAMES TO BOOST ATTENTION & FOCUS\r\n\r\nAttention is one of the essential cognitive functions in our day to day life as the development of attention capacity helps to keep the mind healthy.\r\n\r\nAttention refers to the ability to concentrate on a specific stimulus. It is a cognitive process that is in constant interaction with other domains such as memory.\r\n\r\nThis collection of puzzles is developed in collaboration with doctors and experts in neuropsychology. You will find games aimed at working the different types of attention:\r\n\r\nSelective or focalized attention: Ability to attend to a stimulus ignoring the rest of irrelevant stimuli.\r\nDivided or changing attention: ability to change the focus of attention from one task to another.\r\nSustained attention: ability to maintain concentration in a task for a certain time.\r\n\r\n\r\nABOUT TELLMEWOW\r\n\r\nTellmewow is a mobile game development company specialized in easy adaptation and basic usability which makes our games ideal for the elderly or young people who simply want to play an occasional game without major complications.\r\n\r\nIf you have any suggestions for improvement or want to stay tuned about upcoming games, follow us on our social networks.",
